From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <dev@luneos.org>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 16:55:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] technology: add TetheringIPAddress and TetheringChannel,
 allow open AP

webos-connman-adapter drives WiFi tethering through three properties
that upstream ConnMan does not have:

  - TetheringIPAddress, the address the AP itself takes, from which the
    served /24 is derived.  Upstream always asks the IP pool for a free
    block, so the address could not be pinned down.
  - TetheringChannel, the 802.11 channel.  Upstream 2.0 gained
    TetheringFreq for the same purpose, so rather than carrying a second
    field this maps channel to frequency and keeps tethering_freq as the
    single source of truth.  Both properties are exported and either can
    be set.
  - An empty TetheringPassphrase, which is how the adapter's
    securityType=open mode asks for an open AP.  plugins/wifi.c already
    turns an empty passphrase into G_SUPPLICANT_SECURITY_NONE; only the
    D-Bus side rejected it.

Reworked from the webOS OSE ConnMan fork, which duplicated the whole of
__connman_tethering_set_enabled() to support the static address.  Here
the existing function takes an optional address instead, so the two
paths cannot drift apart, and the derived strings are released on every
exit path.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
 src/connman.h    |   2 +-
 src/technology.c | 140 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/tethering.c  | 130 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 3 files changed, 244 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

